# Terraform
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Real values: object IDs and backend coordinates are tenant-specific.
# The .example files are what belongs in git.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
backend.hcl
!backend.hcl.example
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
# Lock files are excluded here and should be committed after your first
# `terraform init` against the public registry. They are absent because the
# environment this repository was authored in had no route to
# registry.terraform.io, and a lock file generated from a local provider mirror
# carries only one platform's hash - committing that would break `init` for
# everyone else. Run `terraform init`, then:
#   git add -f terraform/environments/*/.terraform.lock.hcl
# Module directories genuinely do not need one; only root modules do.
**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

